---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro'

const roles = [
  { org: 'Nura', role: 'Backend architecture for an AI journaling app', when: '2025' },
  { org: 'Intosoft', role: 'Backend engineer on search, real-time, and billing', when: '2024–2025' },
  { org: 'Yatri Design Studio', role: 'Software engineer on EV charging admin and inventory', when: '2023–2024' },
  { org: 'Leapfrog Technology', role: 'Software engineer intern', when: '2022' },
]
---

<Base title="About" description="Bishal Hona, a product-minded backend engineer with about three years building Node and TypeScript systems, who has gone deep on the infrastructure behind AI products.">
  <section class="shell ab-head">
    <p class="label">About</p>
    <h1 class="display ab-title measure">
      I'm a backend engineer. I've gone deep on the layer between a model's API
      and the person waiting on the other end.
    </h1>
  </section>

  <section class="shell ab-body">
    <div class="ab-prose measure flow">
      <p>
        I've spent about three years building Node and TypeScript backends.
        Somewhere in there I realized the prompt is rarely the hard part of an AI
        product. The hard part is everything around it. Keeping background jobs
        from taking each other down when one of them fails. Holding onto a user's
        history so it still makes sense to the model months later. Getting
        responses to stream so the app feels alive. Making the auth hold up when
        someone actually pokes at it.
      </p>
      <p>
        I care most about the parts of a system you never notice when they're
        working. I keep orchestration, tool calls, and storage cleanly separated,
        and I do it for a practical reason: it lets me think through what happens
        when something fails before it does. I try to build things that
        stay calm when they break. And I try to leave enough of a trail that the
        next person can follow why I did what I did.
      </p>
      <p>
        I don't do model training or MLOps. I work across the product backend,
        and I've gone deepest on the part that sits between the model and the
        person using it, which is where a lot of AI apps succeed or fail.
      </p>
      <p>
        AI has made me a lot faster, but it hasn't done the thinking for me, and
        I don't expect it to.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="ab-side">
      <p class="label ab-side__label">Background</p>
      <ul class="ab-timeline">
        {roles.map((r) => (
          <li class="ab-role">
            <span class="ab-role__when label">{r.when}</span>
            <span class="ab-role__org mono">{r.org}</span>
            <span class="ab-role__desc">{r.role}</span>
          </li>
        ))}
      </ul>

      <p class="label ab-side__label ab-side__label--2">Working with</p>
      <p class="ab-stack mono">
        Node · TypeScript · PostgreSQL · MongoDB · Redis · BullMQ · Socket.IO · Docker · AWS
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .ab-head { padding-top: clamp(2rem, 1.5rem + 3vw, 4rem); }
  .ab-title {
    font-size: var(--step-2);
    line-height: 1.22;
    letter-spacing: 0.01em;
    margin-top: 0.8rem;
  }

  .ab-body {
    margin-top: clamp(2.5rem, 1.5rem + 4vw, 4.5rem);
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1.6fr 1fr;
    gap: clamp(2rem, 1rem + 4vw, 5rem);
    align-items: start;
  }
  .ab-prose p { font-family: var(--font-sans); font-size: var(--step-1); line-height: 1.65; color: var(--graphite); }
  .ab-prose b { color: var(--ink); }

  .ab-side { position: sticky; top: 2rem; }
  .ab-side__label { display: block; margin-bottom: 1.1rem; }
  .ab-side__label--2 { margin-top: 2.4rem; }

  .ab-timeline {
    list-style: none; padding: 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column;
    border: 1px solid var(--ink);
  }
  .ab-role {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    gap: 0.15rem;
    padding: 0.9rem 1rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--ink);
  }
  .ab-role:first-child { border-top: 0; }
  .ab-role__when { color: var(--rust); }
  .ab-role__org { color: var(--ink); font-size: var(--step-0); }
  .ab-role__desc { color: var(--graphite); font-size: var(--step--1); line-height: 1.45; }

  .ab-stack {
    color: var(--graphite); font-size: var(--step--1); line-height: 1.9;
    letter-spacing: 0.01em;
    padding: 0.9rem 1rem; border: 1px solid var(--ink); background: var(--panel);
  }

  @media (max-width: 46rem) {
    .ab-body { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .ab-side { position: static; }
  }
</style>
